Time passes.

Marsh feeds an oilcloth packet into the stove.

> examine stove
examine stove

Fresh ash on the grate. One scrap did not burn: a corner with half of the company's stamp.

You write it in your notebook: someone burned the company's paper.

> accuse marsh
accuse marsh

You tell Marsh what you know. He asks for the pages, and you do not have them.

Charged, case weak

Marsh is charged with the murder of Amos Reed. Without the true pages, his counsel will make a meal of it. The ash in the stove is all that is left of them.